  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>Southwest Minnesota State University is a public university in Marshall, Minnesota. It is part of the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities System. It attracts approximately 232 international students from over 27 countries annually.</p><p>The University has approximately 8,700 students and employs 148 faculty members.</p>  <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>The campus of Southwest Minnesota State University is lively and varied as students have registered over 70 student clubs that range from cultural organisations to social justice collectives. Students can access the Success Center to find support services ranging from mental health to career help. The fitness center on campus has cardio and weight equipment, a rock climbing wall, and a pool. There are also intramural sports and outdoor recreation opportunities.</p>"
    ],
